    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as the clear engine of our offense, carrying an elite score of 76.19. His matchup against Michael McGreevy (4.43 xERA) is the most favorable on the board, and we are heavily leaning into his dynamic platoon advantage (+6%) and the anticipated spot in the three-hole to maximize his production. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains our secondary pillar at 66.63; despite a neutral park factor, the right-handed matchup against Troy Melton presents a perfect environment for his high-contact profile, with his projected order spot in the heart of the lineup providing a strong cushion for RBI potential.\n\nWe faced a tight decision between **Austin Riley** (53.73) and our bench depth, but with our current bench consisting of players like **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak** currently sidelined by off-days, our bench optimization was simplified. **Zach McKinstry** (55.54) earns the start over fringe options primarily due to the soft matchup against Randy Dobnak (5.65 xERA), which outweighs the drag of his #7 spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Travis Bazzana** (47.51) and **Gabriel Moreno** (60.15) round out the lineup as reliable contributors. Note that both **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags; while we are comfortable with our projections for **Gabriel Moreno**, any significant drop in his order position would be the primary risk to his current efficiency score. We will continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** for late-week pivot opportunities should these primary starters underperform or face weather-related delays.",
